    {
      "id": 224640,
      "name": "Kratos13",
      "username": "Kratos13",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/65b543/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2018-12-14T01:57:46.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Is it too soon to start the hype train yet? &nbsp;I’m extremely curious on how Handelabra will implement the UI for&nbsp;certain things from Oblivaeon.</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Applied Numerology. &nbsp;Seriously, how will the UI work here to choose one number on a card power&nbsp;and increase or decrease it? &nbsp;I suppose it could be a series of prompts&nbsp;like Twist the Ether, but I’m curious if there’s a better way.</li>\n\t<li>Maria Helena’s Plot. &nbsp;Look at the bottom card of your deck at any time. &nbsp;New button somewhere? &nbsp;Or bottom card will be shown at the top/side or something when you click on her deck?</li>\n\t<li>Akash’Thriya. &nbsp;Lots of her cards allow her to either play or discard the top card if the environment deck. &nbsp;On the tabletop,&nbsp;players can see the card back of the top card of any deck&nbsp;and therefore can make an informed decision on whether to play or discard (i.e., whether it’s an Akash card or Environment card). &nbsp;So far Handelbra hasn’t implemented this ability (to spot Shinobi Assassins) but probably didn’t need to (the game will prompt/warn the player who is about to draw a Shinobi Assassin). &nbsp;However, I think it’s crucial for an Akash player to know what deck the top environment card belongs to and hopefully something will be implemented. &nbsp;If so, what will this look like?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>What else are people looking forward to see?</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:58:05.123Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
